Fix a port race between FPM tests under `make test`.

gh24046-stdio-pipe-double-close.phpt (the test for GHSA-jm4m-qfqx-967m) starts
`sleep 3` in the background from inside an FPM worker. The child inherits the
worker's listening socket and keeps the FPM test port bound for up to 3 seconds
after the test has finished. All FPM tests use the same port, so the next one,
gh8646.phpt, fails with "unable to bind listening socket for address
'127.0.0.1:9008': Address in use" when it starts immediately afterwards.
Waiting at the end of the test lets the child exit first.

Reproduced on php-8.2.36 with `make test` on the two tests in order: 3 of 3 runs
failed without this change, 3 of 3 passed with it.

--- a/sapi/fpm/tests/gh24046-stdio-pipe-double-close.phpt
+++ b/sapi/fpm/tests/gh24046-stdio-pipe-double-close.phpt
@@ -45,6 +45,9 @@
 $tester->terminate();
 $tester->expectNoLogPattern('/unable to (remove|read)/');
 $tester->close();
+/* The background "sleep 3" inherited the FPM listening socket and keeps the port bound
+ * for a few more seconds; wait so the next FPM test (same port) can bind it. */
+sleep(2);
 
 ?>
 Done
